  "track": "track-03",
  "title": "backups recovery migrations availability and practical operations",
  "status": "source-backed-draft-generation-enabled",
  "concepts": [
    "A backup strategy is proven by restore tests. Recovery objectives, retention, encryption, storage separation, and operational ownership must be specified before failure.",
    "Recovery model controls log reuse and point-in-time recovery options. In FULL recovery, the log-backup chain is operationally essential; a missing log backup breaks point-in-time restore coverage.",
    "High availability reduces outage duration; it is not a substitute for backups because replication can propagate accidental deletion or corruption. Synchronous and asynchronous replicas make different latency and data-loss tradeoffs.",
    "Schema changes should be deployed through compatible expand-and-contract steps when old and new application versions may run concurrently.",
    "Temporal tables and change-capture mechanisms preserve different kinds of history; they do not replace a tested database backup and restore plan."
  ],
